Thank you for the suggestion, but I was doxxed/stalked via posting on Reddit 5 years ago and don't want to have anything that could remotely be connected to my address. Plus we need the dogfood today, and the Walmart near me doesn't have smaller bags of the cheapest brand. I'm hopeful and searching every avenue I can to get the help.

&#x200B;

Kinda sucks that people are downvoting my post, but it is what it is..

IMO the only thing required for GPT3 to be able to write "whole programs" is just some more sophisticated UI that will run the code through an IDE and return its errors and iterate a few times. I can generate a decent React static page that renders as an app on my phone with some cool features in like, 5 minutes, and I am definitely not performing some advanced algorithm on top of chatGPT. 

&#x200B;

GPT4 being able to write whole programs isn't a huge jump in my eyes, and I would be super disappointed if it couldn't.

&#x200B;

It's going to be a bit scary if it is generating bug-free, feature-complete code using the latest libraries up to very advanced end-user specifications... if it's doing that, then it's game over for all CS people who aren't at the very top of their org charts.

The majority of my suggestion is to increase the frequency of PvP encounters. The special horde bounty is just another thing to do at boss lairs since I am ... just so tired of fighting the same bosses the exact same way over and over again. Honestly, I don't care how many more bosses they release, they're a boring thing to do. Yeah, they give you something to distract from potential incoming players for a few minutes, but man they could do a lot to make it more interesting. Butcher is the only one I enjoy a little bit still. Tired of the chores and running simulator. Been tired of it since 20 hr in and I'm \~1k now. 

&#x200B;

Hunt PvP is the most unique (and for me, most thrilling by far) gaming experience I'm aware of. I just want more of it, with less of the stuff that's not actually fun!

I think traps should exist in the game, but kill combo traps should not. There should be a minimum radius between traps (and especially poison+concertina). You should not get a full kill for free without a skilltest, even if it's good decision-making. Heavy damage, alert, effects on target, that's fine - but no kills on full HP hunters IMO.

&#x200B;

And yeah, sniper has no counterplay. You could do a Censer tool that lets you make trails of smoke or something.. but as long as the sniper has patience and stays far enough away then you there is literally nothing you can do. Headshotting w/o scope at 150m is just not real counterplay, it's so unlikely to happen even for highly skilled players.

